\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  \cf0 The work is yours, our Lord and God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 the work which is our joy,
\par and since 'tis Yours, God Almighty,
\par no foe can e'er destroy.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Before the wheat-corn can send out
\par to light and life its tender sprout,
\par it in the bosom of the field
\par must first its former nature yield,
\par in death must yield,
\par its former nature yield.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Thro' suffering didst Thou ever, Lord,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj to heaven lift Your eyes
\par O, take all those in one accord
\par with Thee to paradise!
\par Lord, come and fetch Thy children here,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj our share of suffering we will bear;
\par thro' portals of Thy death and pain
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 we gently thro' Thy work attain
\par eternal gain,
\par thro' suffering and thro' pain.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou died for us, O Godly seed,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 transcended death and grave,
\par and would in ample measure feed,
\par they whom their souls would save.
\par Send messengers afar and near.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Let ev'ry one, all nations, hear
\par Thy name, O Lord, praise be to Thee.
\par Prepared to work and wait are we,
\par to work for You,
\par \pard     to work and wait for You!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

